r a chest opacity five years earlier without TB diagnosis or treatment; no glucocorticoid use or family hereditary disease history.\", \"available_at\": \"time_zero\"}], \"unknown_fields\": [\"allergies\", \"complete_home_medication_list\", \"unreported_vital_signs\", \"unreported_numeric_test_values\"]}\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "My primary symptom: Bilateral adrenal nodules found on examination, with biochemical concern for adrenal insufficiency."}, {"role": "user", "content": "To understand what’s going on (and why adrenal insufficiency is suspected), I need a bit more context.\n\n1) What symptoms have you had recently that could fit adrenal insufficiency—fatigue/weakness, weight loss, nausea/vomiting, abdominal pain, dizziness on standing/fainting, salt craving, low appetite?\n\n2) How were the adrenal nodules found (CT/MRI done for what reason), and do you have any history of cancer, tuberculosis/fungal infection, or autoimmune disease (thyroid disease, type 1 diabetes, vitiligo)?\n\nOn exam information available so far: there is **mild hyperpigmentation over the knuckles and knees**, which can be a clue toward **primary adrenal insufficiency** (Addison’s), but we need your symptom story and the imaging context next."}], "max_tokens": 8192, "usage": {"include": true}, "provider": {"order": ["streamlake/fp8"], "allow_fallbacks": false, "require_parameters": true}, "temperature": 0.01, "logprobs": true}, "reservation_usd": "0.01829964", "payload_hash": "8457172a9059d372af25a4646b020f5a4cfb203cf92681507fd44a7d0313cdc8", "ordinal": 0}
